Laya 0.3.5
  https://github.com/NandhaKishorM/laya (release 0.3.5, commit 573e5b6), Apache License 2.0,
  Copyright Convai Innovations. Model weights: convaiinnovations/laya (revision 1c5edc17,
  Apache-2.0), encoder answerdotai/ModernBERT-large. The weights are not redistributed.

  Changes to the vendored Laya code (src/habitus/dm/laya.py, src/habitus/dm/laya_mq.py,
  src/habitus/train/laya*.py), relative to laya/common.py of 0.3.5:
  1. Only DecisionModel (common.py 89-136), build_model (139) and the collate logic (247) are
     vendored, with the same parameter names, so released checkpoints load with strict=True and
     give the same logits on the same inputs.
  2. Nothing is truncated: build_sequence's silent cuts (every option to 48 tokens, options to
     head_max_len - 16, the question, the state to the room left in max_len) are removed. A row over
     2048 tokens, or a question + options head over 256 tokens, is refused, never cut.
  3. Every text segment passes a special-token neutraliser; any special id outside the structural
     positions raises.
  4. The temperature buffer is reset to 1 and the checkpoint's temperature_by_options table is
     dropped; answers are read at T = 1 (fitted temperatures serve calibration reports only).
  5. act_head is kept in the state dict but never run.
  6. Multi-question layout (laya_mq): forward accepts position_ids, a full / sliding attention mask
     dict and a head mask; all are inert when omitted (the original call, bit for bit).

