Qwen3.5 (Qwen/Qwen3.5-4B revision 851bf6e8, Qwen/Qwen3.5-0.8B revision 2fc06364)
  Apache License 2.0. The main decision model is the stock instruction-tuned Qwen3.5-4B read out by
  the logits of its option letters. The local result bundle contains its 6 tokenizer files
  (chat_template.jinja, config.json, merges.txt, tokenizer.json, tokenizer_config.json, vocab.json),
  with copies of this NOTICE and of the Apache-2.0 LICENSE at the bundle root; the weights are not
  redistributed.

ModernBERT (answerdotai/ModernBERT-large)
  Apache License 2.0; the encoder of the Laya decision models. The weights are not redistributed;
  the local result bundle contains the typed-decisions checkpoint's tokenizer files (tokenizer.json,
  tokenizer_config.json) under tokenizer/laya-typed-decisions/, so the laya CPU tests need no weights.

